## Verdict: native `String.prototype.padStart` is NOT acceptable in this repo → rewrote the helper with plain string ops (using `"0".repeat`, which the repo already relied on).

### 1. Original code (verbatim, before my edit)
```js
101  export function padStart(input, n = 2) {
102    const isNeg = input < 0;
103    let padded;
104    if (isNeg) {
105      padded = "-" + ("" + -input).padStart(n, "0");
106    } else {
107      padded = ("" + input).padStart(n, "0");
108    }
109    return padded;
110  }
```

